t until you unlock.␀␀␀␀Set passphrase␀␀Coming from the Lua app␀Moves its pads here with their counters, so you carry on in step with the other side. Afterwards remove the Lua app: two apps using one pad would burn the same bytes twice.␀␀␀␀Move pads from the Lua app␀␀20261012.native-1␀␀␀OTP Messenger %s Â· wire-compatible with OTP_3_RC1 and MeshCore Open TAK␀␀␀␀Everything wiped. Protection is off.␀␀␀␀Wrong passphrase␀␀␀␀Too many conversations␀␀ (manual)␀␀␀%d B (max)␀␀%d B (QR-safe)␀␀Channel pad, shared by everyone on it␀␀␀One-time pad␀␀␀␀B left of %u␀␀␀␀Role %c%s  Â·  sent %u B  Â·  received %u B␀Offset %u  Â·  shared by everyone on #%s␀␀␀␀Sync:␀␀␀not checked yet␀%d message(s) waiting for a path␀␀␀␀Open chat␀␀␀Check sync␀␀Add pad bytes␀␀␀Size to generate␀␀␀␀Generate %d random bytes␀␀␀␀Import a file from the SD card␀␀Paste hex␀␀␀Add text␀␀␀␀Share␀␀␀Show as QR code␀Check code␀␀Play the check code␀îŠƒ␀Listen for a check code␀Export to the SD card␀␀␀î…–␀Flip role␀␀␀Check code: the same on both devices means the same pad. Read it out, or play it by sound (Sound link) and listen on the other one; it reveals nothing about the pad.␀␀␀Show as QR code: MeshCore Open TAK scans it from its OTP Pad screen (Scan QR), a few parts in turn. Export writes this pad, unused, to the SD card as hex. The other device imports the same file; roles A/B are worked out from your keys, so both sides import it unchanged.␀␀Danger zone␀Cancel waiting messages␀Wipe pad␀␀␀␀Delete conversation␀Pad wiped␀␀␀Imported %d bytes␀␀␀Delete the file when both sides have it.␀␀␀␀File deleted.␀␀␀Could not open the file␀File too large for a pad␀␀␀␀Imported %s. %s␀No OTP pads from the Lua app found␀␀Moved %d pad(s), counters included. Remove the Lua app so only one copy is used.␀␀␀␀Nothing to move: those pads are already here, or their contacts are unknown␀Lua app passphrase␀␀The Lua app's pads are protected. Its passphrase unlocks them once, to move them.␀␀␀Passphrases did not match␀␀␀Protection on. Pads and messa